  37:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_partial_f32.c ****  *
  38:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_partial_f32.c ****  * Partial Convolution is equivalent to Convolution except that a subset of the output samples is g
  39:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_partial_f32.c ****  * Each function has two additional arguments.
  40:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_partial_f32.c ****  * <code>firstIndex</code> specifies the starting index of the subset of output samples.
  41:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_partial_f32.c ****  * <code>numPoints</code> is the number of output samples to compute.
  42:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_partial_f32.c ****  * The function computes the output in the range
  43:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_partial_f32.c ****  * <code>[firstIndex, ..., firstIndex+numPoints-1]</code>.
  44:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_partial_f32.c ****  * The output array <code>pDst</code> contains <code>numPoints</code> values.
  45:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_partial_f32.c ****  *
  46:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_partial_f32.c ****  * The allowable range of output indices is [0 srcALen+srcBLen-2].
  47:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_partial_f32.c ****  * If the requested subset does not fall in this range then the functions return ARM_MATH_ARGUMENT_
  48:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_partial_f32.c ****  * Otherwise the functions return ARM_MATH_SUCCESS.
  49:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_partial_f32.c ****  * \note Refer arm_conv_f32() for details on fixed point behavior.
  50:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_partial_f32.c ****  *
  51:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_partial_f32.c ****  *
  52:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_partial_f32.c ****  * <b>Fast Versions</b>
  53:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_partial_f32.c ****  *
  54:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_partial_f32.c ****  * \par
  55:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_partial_f32.c ****  * Fast versions are supported for Q31 and Q15 of partial convolution.  Cycles for Fast versions ar
  56:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_partial_f32.c ****  * the input signals should be scaled down to avoid intermediate overflows.
  57:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_partial_f32.c ****  *
  58:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_partial_f32.c ****  *
  59:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_partial_f32.c ****  * <b>Opt Versions</b>
  60:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_partial_f32.c ****  *
  61:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_partial_f32.c ****  * \par
  62:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_partial_f32.c ****  * Opt versions are supported for Q15 and Q7.  Design uses internal scratch buffer for getting good
  63:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_partial_f32.c ****  * These versions are optimised in cycles and consumes more memory(Scratch memory) compared to Q15 
  64:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_conv_partial_f32.c ****  */
